<urn:usf:contract:naming-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Close the naming normalisation debt at its cause. Register a delete operation in the semantic transaction so a graph source can be moved, and stop the operator-facing command surface calling the foundation \"core\"." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
<urn:usf:contract:naming-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objectiveEvidence> "Two filenames still read anqr-first-slice and hermes-management while both graph identities are correct, because usf transact admits only append-quads, write-file and derive-economics-projection: with no delete, and a postimage validator that correctly refuses a two-copy state, a source move cannot be expressed as a transaction. Separately, usf help describes a resource-scoped \"core dependency closure\" and a \"core authority profile\", using for the foundation the one word the naming standard retires for it." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
<urn:usf:contract:naming-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:constructionRouteConstraint> "Local, hermetic and deterministic. It contacts no provider, reads no credential, provisions nothing, and writes only the declared paths." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
