<urn:usf:contract:naming-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A delete operation lets a transaction remove a declared path. It does not weaken the postimage guarantee: the deletion is part of the proposed postimage and the resulting corpus is validated before any path is written, which is exactly why the two-copy state was refused." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
<urn:usf:contract:naming-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Renaming prose in the command surface changes no behaviour, no output schema and no reason code. It is included here because it is the same debt from the same standard, and a second lane for two sentences would cost more than it saved." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
