<urn:usf:requirement:naming-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A semantic transaction must be able to delete a declared path, so that moving a graph source is expressible as one atomic transaction whose validated postimage contains neither a missing source nor two copies of one. The operator-facing command surface must not name the foundation \"core\"." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
<urn:usf:requirement:naming-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "A deletion is part of the proposed postimage and is validated with it; a moved source never exists twice." <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
<urn:usf:requirement:naming-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:naming-completion> .
